cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software archive and the accompanying article."
title: "EnzSub: enzyme-domain continued pre-training and substrate-aware training for enzyme representation learning"
abstract: >-
  Source code and experiment configurations for enzyme-domain continued pre-training (CPT),
  substrate-aware training (SUB), representation analyses and downstream numerical evaluations
  reported in the accompanying manuscript "Substrate supervision reorganizes protein language
  model representations of enzymes by catalytic identity".
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AGI-FBHC/EnzSub"
url: "https://github.com/AGI-FBHC/EnzSub"
keywords:
  - enzyme representation
  - protein language model
  - substrate supervision
  - enzyme function prediction
  - continued pre-training
